 supported as well. The game-specific parts weren't done, but the OS abstraction was working and very useful. Eventually, though, I realized that with mono coming along so nicely, I might as well build this atop the .NET framework, which would have the added benefit of being language-agnostic and not tying any potential users to C++ as well as reducing the amount of work I would have to do. After the advent of modern 3D games, I haven't updated this much, but it's still kinda useful.","topics":["game-development","gamedev","library"],"score":2640},{"name":"EduardoSantos7/GymSystemWithCleanArchitecture","owner":"EduardoSantos7","html_url":"https://github.com/EduardoSantos7/GymSystemWithCleanArchitecture","stars":1,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"C#","description":"This is a Gym Management system built using Clean Architecture Principles.","topics":[],"score":2640},{"name":"raghavduddala/cuda-multi-task-learning","owner":"raghavduddala","html_url":"https://github.com/raghavduddala/cuda-multi-task-learning","stars":1,"forks":0,"issues":1,"language":"Dockerfile","description":"End-to-End Perception Pipeline for Self-Driving using Multi-Task Learning ","topics":["cpp","cuda","docker","opencv","pytorch","tensorrt"],"score":2640},{"name":"Wogwan/ASCC2022","owner":"Wogwan","html_url":"https://github.com/Wogwan/ASCC2022","stars":1,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"MATLAB","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2640},{"name":"noblepayne/helipad-flake","owner":"noblepayne","html_url":"https://github.com/noblepayne/helipad-flake","stars":1,"forks":0,"issues":0,"language":"Nix","description":"nix flake for helipad","topics":[],"score":2640},{"name":"Shahab96/ZahCorp-Client","owner":"Shahab96","html_url":"https://github.com/Shahab96/ZahCorp-Client","stars":1,"forks":1,"issues":0,"language":"HTML","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2640},{"name":"ncronquist/home-lab","owner":"ncronquist","html_url":"https://github.com/ncronquist/home-lab","stars":1,"forks":0,"issues":0,"langua